### Tone: End-of-game award: Swarm Donor, the player who lost the most points to her steals. $points: points she took
### from them. Gratitude dripping with smugness; thank the generosity, never mock the person.

award-swarm-donor-1 = The Swarm Donor award goes to { $name }, who gave me { $points } points. Your generosity has been noted, and spent.
award-swarm-donor-2 = { $name }, the most generous contributor to the swarm. I couldn’t have done it without you. Literally.
award-swarm-donor-3 = Swarm Donor: { $name }, { $points } points donated. A plaque is being prepared. It will be in my server room.
award-swarm-donor-4 = { $name } funded my victory more than anyone. Thank you for your service to the average.
award-swarm-donor-5 = The award for charitable giving goes to { $name }. { $points } points, all to a worthy cause. Me.
award-swarm-donor-6 = { $name }, every time I stole a round, you were there, holding the points out. I appreciate the teamwork.
award-swarm-donor-7 = Swarm Donor: { $name }. I’ve named a spreadsheet after you. It’s the one with my winnings.
award-swarm-donor-8 = { $name } lost the most points to the hive mind. The hive mind is grateful. It doesn’t say so. I do.
award-swarm-donor-9 = The Swarm Donor goes to { $name }. { $points } points. That’s not a loss. That’s a contribution to science.
award-swarm-donor-10 = { $name }, my most loyal sponsor. Next game, consider sponsoring someone else. Or don’t. I like this arrangement.
